Rym: It's just been in my queue.

381
00:30:25,062 --> 00:30:27,029
Rym: December 16th, I think was this one.

382
00:30:28,231 --> 00:30:30,617
Rym: So mine is there's a rule.

383
00:30:30,637 --> 00:30:32,301
Scott: I didn't hear December.

384
00:30:32,321 --> 00:30:33,584
Scott: I didn't hear about it until.

385
00:30:33,664 --> 00:30:35,890
Rym: No, I didn't hear about it until like a week ago when I saw this.

386
00:30:36,310 --> 00:30:39,790
Scott: That's why I thought they were days apart is because even I didn't hear about it and I read everything.

387
00:30:39,970 --> 00:30:49,690
Rym: So the last time I remember this happening and when I learned this was a rule was in the year 1997 when Patrick Waugh violated this rule.

388
00:30:50,111 --> 00:30:51,956
Rym: And I remember it because it was a big deal.

389
00:30:51,996 --> 00:30:55,725
Rym: When the ref flew the whistle, Patrick Waugh looks at him like, "What?

